# Review: KanbanPlugin

The data model matches the spec: `Kanban` (`org.dxos.type.kanban@0.2.0`) holds an `Arrangement` and a
`spec` union of view and items variants. Layout, drag and drop, and add-card are exercised by the board
model browser test, the arrangement unit tests and a Playwright smoke spec against the mutable-schema
story. The four ops are registered with undo mappings, but no test invokes them. The gaps that matter:
`deleteCardField` is never invoked from the UI (the article has no remove-field action), so F-4.3 is only
reachable via undo plumbing; the AI skill contributes instructions with an empty tool list, so an agent cannot
create boards or move cards (F-7.2); and the items variant has no add-card and a no-op remove, so the two
variants do not share card management. The settings component is named `KanbanProperties`. Scenarios T-1,
T-5, T-6 and T-7 have no automation. `deus review items` lists only the first test of the QA block, so
QA-2 (showcase clip) has no verdict here.

## Extensions

